<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Shattuara II</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">13th century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century-bce">13th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Shattuara II was the last known king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mitanni">Mitanni</a>, or <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hanigalbat">Hanigalbat</a>, in the 13th century BCE. Allied with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hittite-empire">Hittites</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ahlamu">Ahlamu</a>, he rebelled against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assyrian-empire">Assyria</a> but was defeated by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shalmaneser-i">Shalmaneser I</a>, who claimed to have blinded 14,400 captives and annexed his kingdom. His defeat ended Mitanni as an independent state.</p></div>
